27950      title 'Gasoline and Emissions Data';
27951      data gas;
27952      set sashelp.gas;
27953      if fuel in ('Ethanol', '82rongas', 'Gasohol');
27954      run;

NOTE: There were 171 observations read from the data set SASHELP.GAS.
NOTE: The data set WORK.GAS has 112 observations and 4 variables.

27955      ods graphics on;
27956      * Request a Spline Transformation of Equivalence Ratio;
27957      proc transreg data=Gas solve ss2 plots=(transformation obp residuals);
27958      model identity(nox) = spline(EqRatio / nknots=4);
27959      run;

NOTE: 2 observations were deleted from the analysis due to missing values.
NOTE: Algorithm converged.
NOTE: There were 112 observations read from the data set WORK.GAS.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE TRANSREG printed page 1721.

27960      * Separate Curves and Intercepts;
27961      proc transreg data=Gas solve ss2 additive plots=(transformation obp);
27962      model identity(nox) = class(Fuel / zero=none) |
27963      spline(EqRatio / nknots=4 after);
27964      run;

NOTE: Since the model contains SMOOTH, BSPLINE, PBSPLINE, or a CLASS expansion with ZERO=NONE, a model with an implicit intercept is fit.
NOTE: All statistics are mean corrected.
NOTE: 2 observations were deleted from the analysis due to missing values.
NOTE: Algorithm converged.
NOTE: There were 112 observations read from the data set WORK.GAS.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE TRANSREG printed page 1722.

27965      * Separate Intercepts;
27966      proc transreg data=Gas solve ss2 additive;
27967      model identity(nox) = class(Fuel / zero=none)
27968      spline(EqRatio / nknots=4);
27969      run;

NOTE: Since the model contains SMOOTH, BSPLINE, PBSPLINE, or a CLASS expansion with ZERO=NONE, a model with an implicit intercept is fit.
NOTE: All statistics are mean corrected.
NOTE: 2 observations were deleted from the analysis due to missing values.
NOTE: Algorithm converged.
NOTE: There were 112 observations read from the data set WORK.GAS.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE TRANSREG printed page 1723.

27970      * Separate Curves and Intercepts with Penalized B-Splines;
27971      proc transreg data=Gas ss2 plots=transformation lprefix=0;
27972      model identity(nox) = class(Fuel / zero=none) * pbspline(EqRatio);
27973      run;

NOTE: AFTER is assumed when PBSPLINE is crossed with a CLASS variable.
NOTE: Since the model contains SMOOTH, BSPLINE, PBSPLINE, or a CLASS expansion with ZERO=NONE, a model with an implicit intercept is fit.
NOTE: All statistics are mean corrected.
NOTE: 2 observations were deleted from the analysis due to missing values.
NOTE: Algorithm converged.
NOTE: There were 112 observations read from the data set WORK.GAS.
